INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Lunges', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright holding two haltères in vos mains by your sides. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Step forward with your right leg around 2 feet or so from the foot being left stationary behind and lower your upper body down, while keeping the torse upright and maintaining balance. Inspirez as you go down. Note: As in the other exercises, do not allow your genou to go forward beyond your toes as you come down, as this will put undue stress on the genou joint. Make sure that you keep your front shin perpendiculaire à the ground.
3. Using mainly the heel of your foot, push up and go back to the position de départ as you expirez.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform with the left leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lunges/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Lying One-Arm Rear Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. While holding a haltère in one hand, lay with your poitrine down on a slightly inclined (around 15 degrees when measured from le sol) adjustable banc. The other hand can be used to hold to the leg of the banc for stability.
2. Position the palm of the hand that is holding the haltère in a neutral manner (paumes vers your torse) as you keep the arm extended with the coude slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now raise the arm with the haltère to the side until your coude is at épaule height and your arm is roughly parallèle au sol as you expirez. Conseil : Maintain your arm perpendiculaire à the torse while keeping your arm extended throughout le mouvement. Also, keep the contraction at the top for a second.
4. Lentement, lower the haltère to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_One-Arm_Rear_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Lying Pronation', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat face down with one arm holding a haltère and the other hand on top of the banc folded so that you can rest votre tête on it.
2. Bend the coudes of the arm holding the haltère so that it creates a angle de 90 degrés between the upper arm and the forearm.
3. Now raise the upper arm so that the forearm is perpendiculaire à le sol and the upper arm is perpendiculaire à your torse. Conseil : The upper arm should be parallèle au sol and also creating a angle de 90 degrés with your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, externally rotate your forearm so that the haltère is lifted forward as you maintain the angle de 90 degrés bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is parallèle au sol. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.
5. As you Inspirez, Lentement, go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Pronation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Lying Rear Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. While holding a haltère in each hand, lay with your poitrine down on a slightly inclined (around 15 degrees when measured from le sol) adjustable banc.
2. Position the palms of the hands in a neutral manner (paumes vers your torse) as you keep the arms extended with the coudes slightly bent. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now raise the arms to the side until your coudes are at épaule height and vos bras are roughly parallèle au sol as you expirez. Conseil : Maintain vos bras perpendiculaire à the torse while keeping them extended throughout le mouvement. Also, keep the contraction at the top for a second.
4. Lentement, lower the haltères to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then switch to the other arm.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Rear_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Lying Supination', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Lie sideways on a flat banc with one arm holding a haltère and the other hand on top of the banc folded so that you can rest votre tête on it.
2. Bend the coudes of the arm holding the haltère so that it creates a angle de 90 degrés between the upper arm and the forearm.
3. Now raise the upper arm so that the forearm is parallèle au sol and perpendiculaire à your torse (Conseil : So the forearm will be directly in front of you). The upper arm will be stationary by your torse and should be parallèle au sol (aligned with your torse en permanence). C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, externally rotate your forearm so that the haltère is lifted up in a semicircle motion as you maintain the angle de 90 degrés bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is perpendiculaire à le sol and the torse pointing towards the ceiling. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.
5. As you Inspirez, Lentement, go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then switch to the other arm.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Lying_Supination/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell One-Arm Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère and either sit on a military press banc or a utility banc that has a back support on it as you place the haltères upright on top of your cuisses or Levez-vous straight.
2. Clean the haltère up to bring it to épaule height. The other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist or grabbing a fixed surface.
3. Rotate the poignet so that the palm of your hand is facing forward. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you expirez, push the haltère up until your arm is fully extended.
5. Après une pause, Lentement, come down back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then switch arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell One-Arm Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère and either sit on a military press banc or a utility banc that has a back support on it as you place the haltères upright on top of your cuisses or Levez-vous straight.
2. Clean the haltère up to bring it to épaule height and then extend the arm over votre tête so that the whole arm is perpendiculaire à le sol and next to votre tête. The haltère should be on top of you. The other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist, supporting the upper arm that has the haltère or grabbing a fixed surface.
3. Rotate the poignet so that the palm of your hand is facing forward and the pinkie is facing the ceiling. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lentement, lower the haltère behind votre tête as you hold the upper arm stationary. Inspirez as you perform this movement and pause when your triceps are fully stretched.
5. Revenez en position de départ by flexing your triceps as you Expirez. Conseil : It is imperative that only the forearm moves. The upper arm should remain en permanence stationary next to votre tête.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and switch arms.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell One-Arm Upright Row', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère and Tenez-vous debout avec your arm extended in front of you with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos straight. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : The haltère should be resting on top of your cuisse with the palm of vos mains facing your cuisses.
2. Keep the other hand can be kept fully extended to the side, by the waist or grabbing a fixed surface. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Use your side épaules to lift the haltère as you expirez. The haltère should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until the haltère is nearly in line with your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the haltère, your coude should always be higher than your forearm. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
4. Lower the haltère back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and switch arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_One-Arm_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Prone Incline Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère on each hand and lie face down on an incline banc with your épaules near top of the incline. Your genous can rest on the seat or vos jambes can be straddled to the sides (my preferred way).
2. Let vos bras extend and hang naturally in front of you so that they are perpendiculaire à le sol.
3. Now keep your coudes in by your side and face the palms forward. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise the haltères by contracting the biceps until vos bras are fully flexed. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement and ensure that only the forearms move. The upper arms should remain stationary en permanence.
5. Lower the haltères until vos bras are fully extended.
6. Répétez for the recommended amount of times.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Prone_Incline_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère in each arm and Tenez-vous debout avec vos bras extended by your sides with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos straight. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : The haltère should be next to your cuisses with the palm of vos mains facing back.
2. Use your side épaules to lift the haltères as you expirez. The haltères should be to the side of the body as you move them up. Continue to lift it until the haltères are nearly in line with your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the haltère, your coude should always be higher than your forearm. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement.
3. Lower the haltères back down Lentement, to the position de départ. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Rear Lunge', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright holding two haltères in vos mains by your sides. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Step backward with your right leg around two feet or so from the left foot and lower your upper body down, while keeping the torse upright and maintaining balance. Inspirez as you go down. Conseil : As in the other exercises, do not allow your genou to go forward beyond your toes as you come down, as this will put undue stress on the genou joint. Make sure that you keep your front shin perpendiculaire à the ground. Keep the torse upright during the lunge; flexible hanche flexors are important. A long lunge emphasizes the Gluteus Maximus; a short lunge emphasizes quadriceps.
3. Push up and go back to the position de départ as you expirez. Conseil : Use the ball of vos pieds to push in order to accentuate the quadriceps. To focus on the fessiers, press with your heels.
4. Now Répétez with the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Rear_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Scaption', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. This corrective exercise strengthens the muscles that stabilize your omoplates. Hold a light poids in each hand, hanging at your sides. Your thumbs should pointing up.
2. Begin le mouvement raising vos bras out in front of you, about 30 degrees off center. vos bras should be fully extended as you perform le mouvement.
3. Continue until vos bras are parallel to the ground, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Scaption/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Seated Box Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Position a box a couple feet to the side of a banc. Hold a haltère to your poitrine with both hands and seat yourself on the banc facing the box. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Plant vos pieds firmly on the ground as you lean forward, extending through the hanches and genous to jump up and forward.
3. Land on the box with both feet, absorbing the impact by allowing the hanches and genous to bend.
4. Step down and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Seated_Box_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Seated One-Leg Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Haltères', '1. Place a block on le sol about 12 inches from a flat banc.
2. Sit on a flat banc and place a haltère on your upper left cuisse about 3 inches above your genou.
3. Now place the ball of your left foot on the block. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise your toes up as high as possible as you expirez and you contract your calf muscle. Hold the contraction for a second.
5. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ, stretching as far down as possible.
6. Répétez for your prescribed number of repetitions and then Répétez with the right leg.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Seated_One-Leg_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. While holding a haltère in each hand, sit on a military press banc or utility banc that has back support. Place the haltères upright on top of your cuisses.
2. Now raise the haltères to épaule height one at a time using your cuisses to help propel them up into position.
3. Make sure to rotate your poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing forward. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Now, expirez and push the haltères upward until they touch at the top.
5. Then, Après une pause, at the top contracted position, Lentement, lower the poids back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Haltères', '1. Stand erect with a haltère on each hand (paumes vers your torse), arms extended on the sides.
2. Lift the haltères by elevating the épaules as high as possible while you expirez. Hold the contraction at the top for a second. Conseil : The arms should remain extended en permanence. Refrain from using the biceps to help lift the haltères. Only the épaules should be moving up and down.
3. Lower the haltères back to the original position.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Side Bend', 'Abdominaux', 'Haltères', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a haltère on the left hand (paumes vers the torse) as you have the right hand holding your waist. vos pieds should be placed at épaule width. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While keeping votre dos straight and votre tête up, bend only at the waist to the right as far as possible. Inspirez as you bend to the side. Then Maintenez la position 1 seconde and come back up to the position de départ as you expirez. Conseil : Keep the rest of the body stationary.
3. Now Répétez le mouvement but bending to the left instead. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and come back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then change hands.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Side_Bend/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a haltère on each hand (paumes vers the side of vos jambes).
2. Position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section.
3. Begin to Lentement, lower your torse by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until your cuisses are parallèle au sol. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
4. Begin to raise your torse as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Squat To A Bench', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a flat banc behind you while holding a haltère on each hand (paumes vers the side of vos jambes).
2. Position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section.
3. Begin to Lentement, lower your torse by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until you slightly touch the banc behind you. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
4. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Squat_To_A_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Step Ups', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding a haltère on each hand (paumes vers the side of vos jambes).
2. Place the right foot on the elevated platform. Step on the platform by extending the hanche and the genou of your right leg. Use the heel mainly to lift the rest of votre corps up and place the foot of the left leg on the platform as well. Expirez as you execute the force required to come up.
3. Step down with the left leg by flexing the hanche and genou of the right leg as you inspirez. Return to the original standing position by placing the right foot of to next to the left foot on the initial position.
4. Répétez with the right leg for the recommended amount of repetitions and then perform with the left leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Step_Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Tricep Extension -Pronated Grip', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat holding two haltères directly above your épaules. vos bras should be fully extended and form a angle de 90 degrés from your torse and le sol.
2. The palms of vos mains should be facing forward, and your coudes should be tucked in. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now, inspirez and Lentement, lower the haltères until they are near your ears. Be sure to keep your upper arms stationary and your coudes tucked in.
4. Then, expirez and use your triceps to return the poids to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Tricep_Extension_-Pronated_Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dynamic Back Stretch', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping vos bras straight, swing them straight up in front of you 5-10 times, increasing the range of motion each time until vos bras are above votre tête.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dynamic_Back_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dynamic Chest Stretch', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos mains together, arms extended directly in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping vos bras straight, quickly move vos bras back as far as possible and back in again, similar to an exaggerated clapping motion. Répétez 5-10 times, increasing speed as you do so.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dynamic_Chest_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('EZ-Bar Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Levez-vous straight while holding an EZ curl bar at the wide outer handle. The palms of vos mains should be facing forward and slightly tilted inward due to the shape of the bar. Keep your coudes close to your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now, while keeping your upper arms stationary, expirez and curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps. Focus on only moving your forearms.
3. Continue to raise the poids until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Hold the top contracted position for a moment and squeeze the biceps.
4. Then inspirez and Lentement, lower the bar back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/EZ-Bar_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('EZ-Bar Skullcrusher', 'Triceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Using a close grip, lift the EZ bar and hold it with your coudes in as you lie on the banc. vos bras should be perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping the upper arms stationary, lower the bar by allowing the coudes to flex. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Pause once the bar is directly above the forehead.
3. Lift the bar back to the position de départ by extending the coude and exhaling.
4. Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/EZ-Bar_Skullcrusher/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elbow Circles', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Sit or Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds slightly apart.
2. Place vos mains on your épaules with your coudes at épaule level and pointing out.
3. Lentement, make a circle with your coudes. Expirez as you start the circle and Inspirez as you complete the circle.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elbow_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elbow to Knee', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol, crossing your right leg across your bent left genou. Clasp vos mains behind votre tête, beginning with your omoplates on the ground. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Perform the motion by flexing the spine and rotating your torse to bring the left coude to the right genou.
3. Revenez en position de départ and Répétez le mouvement for the desired number of repetitions before switching sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elbow_to_Knee/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elbows Back', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Levez-vous straight.
2. Place both hands on your lower back, fingers pointing downward and coudes out.
3. Then gently pull your coudes back aiming to touch them together.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elbows_Back/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elevated Back Lunge', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Position a bar onto a rack at épaule height loaded to an appropriate poids. Place a short, raised platform behind you.
2. Rack the bar onto your upper back, keeping votre dos arched and tight. Step onto your raised platform with both feet. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by stepping backwards with one leg. Descend by flexing your hanches and genous until your genou touches le sol.
4. Pause, and extend through the hanches and genous to rise up, returning all the way to the position de départ before alternating.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elevated_Back_Lunge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elevated Cable Rows', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Get a platform of some sort (it can be an aerobics or calf raise platform) that is around 4-6 inches in height.
2. Place it on the seat of the cable row machine.
3. Sit down on the machine and place vos pieds on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your genous are slightly bent and not locked.
4. Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of votre dos and grab the V-bar handles.
5. With vos bras extended pull back until your torse is at a angle de 90 degrés from vos jambes. votre dos should be slightly arched and your poitrine should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lats as you hold the bar in front of you. C''est votre position de départ. of the exercise.
6. Keeping the torse stationary, pull the handles back towards your torse while keeping the arms close to it until you touch the abdominals. Expirez as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing votre dos muscles hard. Hold that contraction for a second and Lentement, go back to the original position while breathing in.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elevated_Cable_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Elliptical Trainer', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the elliptical and select the desired option from the menu. Most ellipticals have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.
2. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Elliptical_Trainer/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Exercise Ball Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Lie on an exercise ball with your lower back curvature pressed against the spherical surface of the ball. vos pieds should be bent at the genou and pressed firmly against le sol. The upper torse should be hanging off the top of the ball. The arms should either be kept alongside the body or crossed on top of your poitrine as these positions avoid neck strains (as opposed to the hands behind the back of the head position).
2. Lower your torse into a stretch position keeping the neck stationary en permanence. C''est votre position de départ.
3. With the hanches stationary, flex the waist by contracting the abdominals and curl the épaules and trunk upward until you feel a nice contraction on your abdominals. The arms should simply slide up the side of vos jambes if you have them at the side or just stay on top of your poitrine if you have them crossed. The lower back should always stay in contact with the ball. Expirez as you perform this movement and hold the contraction for a second.
4. As you inspirez, go back to the position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Exercise_Ball_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Exercise Ball Pull-In', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Place an exercise ball nearby and lay on le sol in front of it with vos mains on le sol épaule width apart in a push-up position.
2. Now place your lower shins on top of an exercise ball. Conseil : At this point vos jambes should be fully extended with the shins on top of the ball and the upper body should be in a push-up type of position being supported by your two extended arms in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While keeping votre dos completely straight and the upper body stationary, pull your genous in towards your poitrine as you expirez, allowing the ball to roll forward under your chevilles. Squeeze your abdominaux and hold that position for a second.
4. Now Lentement, straighten vos jambes, rolling the ball back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Exercise_Ball_Pull-In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Extended Range One-Arm Kettlebell Floor Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Kettlebell', '1. Allongez-vous au sol and position a kettlebell for one arm to press. The kettlebell should be held by the handle. The leg on the same side that you are pressing should be bent, with the genou crossing over the midline of the body.
2. Press the kettlebell by extending the coude and adducting the arm, pressing it above votre corps. Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Extended_Range_One-Arm_Kettlebell_Floor_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('External Rotation', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Lie sideways on a flat banc with one arm holding a haltère and the other hand on top of the banc folded so that you can rest votre tête on it.
2. Bend the coudes of the arm holding the haltère so that it creates a angle de 90 degrés between the upper arm and the forearm. Conseil : Keep the arm parallel to your torse.
3. Now bend the coude while keeping the upper arm stationary. In this manner, the forearm will be parallèle au sol and perpendiculaire à your torse (Conseil : So the forearm will be directly in front of you). The upper arm will be stationary by your torse and should be parallèle au sol (aligned with your torse en permanence). C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, externally rotate your forearm so that the haltère is lifted up in a semicircle motion as you maintain the angle de 90 degrés bend between the upper arms and the forearm. You will continue this external rotation until the forearm is perpendiculaire à le sol and the torse pointing towards the ceiling. At this point you will hold the contraction for a second.
5. As you Inspirez, Lentement, go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then switch to the other arm.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/External_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('External Rotation with Band', 'Épaules', 'Élastique', '1. Choke the band around a post. The band should be at the same height as your coude. Tenez-vous debout avec your left side to the band a couple of feet away.
2. Grasp the end of the band with your right hand, and keep your coude pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your coude to keep it firmly in position.
3. With your upper arm in position, your coude should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching across the front of your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Execute le mouvement by rotating your arm in a backhand motion, keeping your coude in place.
5. Continue as far as you are able, pause, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/External_Rotation_with_Band/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('External Rotation with Cable', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the cable to the same height as your coude. Tenez-vous debout avec your left side to the band a couple of feet away.
2. Grasp the handle with your right hand, and keep your coude pressed firmly to your side. We recommend you hold a pad or foam roll in place with your coude to keep it firmly in position.
3. With your upper arm in position, your coude should be flexed to 90 degrees with your hand reaching across the front of your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Execute le mouvement by rotating your arm in a backhand motion, keeping your coude in place.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/External_Rotation_with_Cable/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Face Pull', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Facing a high pulley with a rope or dual handles attached, pull the poids directly towards your face, separating vos mains as you do so. Keep your upper arms parallel to the ground.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Face_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Farmer''s Walk', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. There are various implements that can be used for the farmers walk. These can also be performed with heavy haltères or short bars if these implements aren''t available. Begin by standing between the implements.
2. After gripping the handles, lift them up by driving through your heels, keeping votre dos straight and votre tête up.
3. Walk taking short, quick steps, and don''t forget to breathe. Move for a given distance, typically 50-100 feet, as fast as possible.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Farmers_Walk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Fast Skipping', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start in a relaxed position with one leg slightly forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Skip by executing a step-hop pattern of right-right-step to left-left-step, and so on, alternating back and forth.
3. Perform fast skips by maintaining close contact with the ground and reduce air time, moving as quickly as possible.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Fast_Skipping/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Finger Curls', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your paumes vers up; hands spaced about épaule width.
2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than épaule width apart. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower the bar as far as possible by extending the fingers. Allowing the bar to roll down the hands, catch the bar with the final joint in the fingers.
4. Now curl bar up as high as possible by closing vos mains while exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Finger_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Flat Bench Cable Flyes', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Position a flat banc between two low pulleys so that when you are laying on it, your poitrine will be lined up with the cable pulleys.
2. Lay flat on the banc and keep vos pieds on the ground.
3. Have someone hand you the handles on each hand. You will grab each single handle attachment with a palms up grip.
4. Extend vos bras by your side with a slight bend on your coudes. Conseil : You will keep this bend constant through the whole movement. vos bras should be parallèle au sol. C''est votre position de départ.
5. Now start lifting the arms in a semi-circle motion directly in front of you by pulling the cables together until both hands meet at the top of le mouvement. Squeeze your poitrine as you perform this motion and Expirez during this movement. Also, hold the contraction for a second at the top. Conseil : When performed correctly, at the top position of this movement, vos bras should be perpendiculaire à your torse and le sol touching above your poitrine.
6. Lentement, come back to the position de départ.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Flat_Bench_Cable_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Flat Bench Leg Pull-In', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Lie on an exercise mat or a flat banc with vos jambes off the end.
2. Place vos mains either under your fessiers with your palms down or by the sides holding on to the banc (or with palms down by the side on an exercise mat). Also extend vos jambes straight out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Bend your genous and pull your upper cuisses into your midsection as you Expirez. Continue this movement until your genous are near your poitrine. Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
4. As you Inspirez, Lentement, Revenez en position de départ.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Flat_Bench_Leg_Pull-In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Flat Bench Lying Leg Raise', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Lie with votre dos flat on a banc and vos jambes extended in front of you off the end.
2. Place vos mains either under your fessiers with your palms down or by the sides holding on to the banc. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you keep vos jambes extended, straight as possible with your genous slightly bent but locked raise vos jambes until they make a angle de 90 degrés with le sol. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement and hold the contraction at the top for a second.
4. Now, as you inspirez, Lentement, lower vos jambes back down to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Flat_Bench_Lying_Leg_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Flexor Incline Dumbbell Curls', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Hold the haltère towards the side farther from you so that you have more poids on the side closest to you. (This can be done for a good effect on all biceps haltère exercises). Now do a normal incline haltère curl, but keep your poignets as far back as possible so as to neutralize any stress that is placed on them.
2. Asseyez-vous sur un banc that is angled at 45-degrees while holding a haltère on each hand.
3. Let vos bras hang down on your sides, with the coudes in, and turn the palms of vos mains forward with the thumbs pointing away from the body. Conseil : You will keep this hand position throughout le mouvement as there should not be any twisting of the hands as they come up. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Curl up the two haltères at the same time until your biceps are entièrement contracté and expirez. Conseil : Do not swing the arms or use momentum. Keep a controlled motion en permanence. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the top.
5. As you inspirez, Lentement, go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Flexor_Incline_Dumbbell_Curls/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Floor Glute-Ham Raise', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. You can use a partner for cet exercice or brace vos pieds under something stable.
2. Begin on your genous with your upper legs and torse upright. If using a partner, they will firmly hold vos pieds to keep you in position. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower yourself by extending at the genou, taking care to NOT flex the hanches as you go forward.
